<br>
I dunno, I got a lot of favorites.  I'd have to say that my all-time Weird Al favorite is probably Yoda.  But after that, it depends on my mood.  Jerry Springer and Albequerque are my favorites off of Running with Scissors.  His polkas are always cool.  And UHF was a hillarious movie.  <br>
<br>
I think the genius of Weird Al is that in his parodies, the song matches up with the original almost exactly, but he completely rewrites the words, rather than just changing every 12th word to "givl".  And his "style parodies" (like Dare to be Stupid, which was my first Weird Al album and still one of my favorite songs) mimic different styles so well that if it wasn't so obviously Weird Al, you'd think it was someone else.  <br>
<br>
